{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLq1SmXJvatqnv4QCNiP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the LaTeX printing for unevaluated `1/n`. The change is in `_print_Mul` in `sympy/printing/latex.py`.\n\nThe cause was that an unevaluated `Mul(1, Pow(n, -1))` was printed literally, so `1/20` came out as `1 \\cdot \\frac{1}{20}`. I made that exact shape, with an integer `n`, skip the literal path and print as a normal fraction.\n\nThe two cases from the issue now print as fractions:\n- `(1/20)**(1/30)` gives `\\left(\\frac{1}{20}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{30}}`\n- `(1/1)**(1/1)` gives `\\left(\\frac{1}{1}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{1}}`\n\nThe \"expected\" case `(10/1)**(20/1)` still prints as `\\left(\\frac{10}{1}\\right)^{\\frac{20}{1}}`.\n\n`sympy/printing/tests/test_latex.py` passes (170 passed, 2 xfailed). I didn't add a new test, since the rules say not to touch test files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":882,"cache_read_input_tokens":21934,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":882},"output_tokens":365,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8263b1ed-b7a5-4043-83df-c5e65af657a5","uuid":"f47873c8-74df-4a21-aea0-82c2b06c4b9f","timestamp":"2026-11-24T00:45:14.592Z","request_id":"req_011ChLq1STvGwMBDpnni28MY"}
